---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import CodeWindow from '../components/CodeWindow.astro';
import Closing from '../components/Closing.astro';
---
<Layout title="For developers — FetchX"><div class="container"><div class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow"><Icon name="code" size={17}/> FOR YOUR ENGINEERING TEAM</span><h1>Connect FetchX to the<br/>systems you already use.</h1><p>Start with your data requirements. For qualified workflows, we can scope API access and delivery integrations alongside the managed service.</p></div><div class="developer-body"><CodeWindow/><div class="developer-columns"><div><h2>Define the integration together.</h2><p>During onboarding, we agree the sources, accepted output, authentication, usage limits and delivery behaviour. Your endpoint and credentials are provisioned for that engagement.</p><ul><li><Icon name="check" size={16}/> Source qualification before integration</li><li><Icon name="check" size={16}/> An agreed schema and error handling</li><li><Icon name="check" size={16}/> Usage and access scoped to your workflow</li></ul></div><div><h2>A starting point for your team.</h2><p>The request above is illustrative. <strong>YOUR_PROVISIONED_ENDPOINT</strong> is a placeholder. This marketing website does not serve the customer collection API, and integrations are separately scoped.</p><a class="text-link" style="margin-top:25px" href="https://github.com/karthikbala/FetchX" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Explore the FetchX source <Icon name="diagonal" size={16}/></a></div></div></div></div><Closing/></Layout>
